  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1042 PM MDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nModels continue in good agreement with high pressure anchored over \nthe Desert Southwest through the coming week dominating the weather \npattern, and holding the monsoonal moisture well to the south \nkeeping dry air with pwats less than a half inch over eastern Utah \nand Western Colorado. Troughing across western Canada with a couple \nshortwaves moving through Monday and Tuesday brushing the northern \nareas stronger westerly afternoon winds while keeping the ridge \nflattened over the Southwest. The hot, dry conditions with winds \nflirting with gusts to 25 mph in areas of Western Colorado is \nhinting at localized critical fire weather conditions. Did not issue \nany products on these conditions as they are marginal at this time. \nWill watch these winds over the next few runs for stronger signals. \nStay tuned for updates through the first half of the week. \nOtherwise, look for hot, dry conditions with near record highs \nacross the region, and just isolated showers and thunderstorms along \nthe southern face of the San Juans, especially the eastern San \nJuans.  \n\nFor the latter half of the week, leaning more on the ensemble \nsolutions of the GEFS and European AI as they concur on the \ntroughing to the north shifting to the east, a ridge building on the \nhigh to the southwest north along the West Coast into the Pacific \nnorthwest by mid week. Troughing developing over the Western Pacific \nwill start shifting the pattern east pushing the high east out onto \nthe Plains going into the following week. Confidence is low at more \nthan a week out, but this would be a significant shift to a more \nmonsoonal flow opening the door to the deep moisture over southern \nArizona and northern Mexico moving north into the region. Stay tuned \non this one too.",
